		{"id":"21abab76cdd5a8ec","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_Liquid_Animation2.jpg","x":-8460,"y":1556,"width":704,"height":294},
		{"id":"a89d6dc3d1196d2c","type":"text","text":"Fluid","x":-8235,"y":4181,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"f49f7c1df999b882","type":"text","text":"**Particles and volumes similarities:**\n* Both can be used to represent fuzzy objects\n* Both can be used to describe geometry in-between surfaces or inside surfaces\n\n**Particles and volumes differences:**\n* If very sparse geometry or eye-visible geometry is being modeled (e.g., leafs, snow, rain, etc.) then particles are more efficient\n* If large amount of eye-invisible particles are being modeled (e.g., fog, clouds, smoke, etc.) then volumes are more efficient.\n\n**Particles and volumes for modeling:**\n* Volume of space can be used to store vector field generated using noise, curves or vectors on surface (e.g., tangent field)\n\t* Volume vector field can be used to advect particles in particle system\n* Dynamics of volumetric media can be modeled using physically based methods directly on grid of voxels. \n\t* Result can be converted to particles\n\t* Vector fields computed during simulation can be used as driving force for particles\n* More artistic simulation of volumetric media can be performed using particles and particle system\n\t* Resulting particles can be converted to volume. Example: artistic cloud morphing is easier to perform with a help of particle system than directly using physically based methods.","x":-9117,"y":1953,"width":1187,"height":630},
		{"id":"37c9c34060997741","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim.jpg","x":-8200,"y":1224,"width":446,"height":292},
		{"id":"6042c0d18a2dee95","type":"text","text":"Gas","x":-8346,"y":4355,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e3d381339847f3f4","type":"text","text":"Voxels","x":-8482,"y":4542,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0237bf8351a17d7a","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_Liquid.jpg","x":-8901,"y":1224,"width":663,"height":292},
		{"id":"2108ba3a391776ea","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WN7X9-m4TKQ","x":-4191,"y":901,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"74a1c7629d1667b0","type":"text","text":"When to use it","x":-8628,"y":3987,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a12ae6c8485af5c6","type":"text","text":"VDB","x":-8576,"y":4730,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"1f7728e92f9b3ec4","type":"text","text":"Tutorials:\n* https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RemcySTz6eo\n* https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/pyro-advection/\n* * https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVIlPQO_p2I","x":-8756,"y":5120,"width":481,"height":244,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"143af46ebbf81017","type":"text","text":"Meshing fluid","x":-4160,"y":801,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"65cf2f85ee7bcdab","type":"text","text":"Where it is used","x":-9255,"y":3976,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3514b7c8f1acd1cd","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/GridParticleSim3.jpg","x":-8686,"y":635,"width":400,"height":226},
		{"id":"19522629779a34f7","type":"text","text":"Baking simulation at certain frame gives us possibility to store (freeze) resulting geometry as static.","x":-8996,"y":911,"width":250,"height":187},
		{"id":"67f7d85814db4f0c","type":"text","text":"Dynamics, e.g., smoke:\n* Simulation is performed on voxels which determines density and color information stored per voxel","x":-9017,"y":635,"width":292,"height":211},
		{"id":"3d24137bdf20b71b","type":"text","text":"Static, e.g. static cloud:\n* Density and color information inside voxels is generated using noise","x":-9324,"y":635,"width":272,"height":211},
		{"id":"2daac556eafc4ea6","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/Entagma.png","x":-9346,"y":1174,"width":361,"height":281},
