		{"id":"a3297933fff94b1f","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_Gas.jpg","x":-9344,"y":1709,"width":359,"height":176},
		{"id":"49aac927e02941ca","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/NVIDIA_GVDB_FluidSim_GasShaded.jpg","x":-9344,"y":1495,"width":357,"height":172},
		{"id":"5f57770a9540c634","type":"link","url":"https://graphics.pixar.com/library/ElementalAir/paper.pdf","x":-9457,"y":4185,"width":654,"height":400},
		{"id":"9d501f72df5f5bf8","type":"link","url":"https://graphics.pixar.com/library/ElementalFire/paper.pdf","x":-9457,"y":4660,"width":654,"height":400},
		{"id":"195141be6fbbe479","type":"text","text":"After simulation is finished, voxel/particle representation is triangulated and rendered","x":-8196,"y":615,"width":266,"height":133},
		{"id":"bfcccc4d1997a472","type":"file","file":"Images/Dynamics2/Tools/GridParticleSim2.jpg","x":-8686,"y":416,"width":400,"height":178},
		{"id":"5dbe455c9782e97a","type":"text","text":"Gas:\n* Each voxel contains density and color information (Eulerian approach, since describing gas with particles is unnecessary expensive)","x":-9162,"y":217,"width":290,"height":288},
		{"id":"ff22136580b1802e","type":"text","text":"SideFX tutorials:\n* https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/introduction-to-fluid-simulations/\n* https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/houdini-tutorial-introduction-to-flip-fluids-simply-explained-part-1/","x":-3021,"y":337,"width":561,"height":239},
		{"id":"bfa34f3dd18ba345","type":"text","text":"Liquids:\n* Bulk of a liquid is represented using grid of voxels (Eulerian approach)\n* Top part (e.g., waves, foam, etc.) is represented using points (Lagrangian)","x":-8223,"y":217,"width":320,"height":288},
